# Perfectly Centred Content

```css
.container {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: 100vh;
}
```
Works for modals, hero sections, or splash screens. The container becomes a flex context, and the single child (or grouped children) can be centred both axes.

# Push Footer to Bottom

Use `flex` on the body and a column layout:
```css
body {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  min-height: 100vh;
}
main {
  flex: 1; /* takes remaining space */
}
```
Now `<main>` expands to fill the viewport, pushing `<footer>` to the bottom even if content is short.

# Logo Left, Links Right

```css
.navbar {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
}
```
Place logo in one `<div>` and links in another. The `space-between` pushes them apart. Add `gap` for spacing. Wrap links in a `<ul>` with `display: flex;` to make them horizontal.

# Flex Wrap Creates a Grid

```css
.card-container {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 20px;
}
.card {
  flex: 1 1 300px; /* min 300px, grow/shrink */
}
```
Even with varying content, cards stretch to the same height thanks to default `align-items: stretch;`.
